      "content": "Taking a high dose like 10,000 IU of Vitamin D without professional guidance is risky, especially while on blood thinners like Warfarin. Vitamin D levels need to be monitored by a doctor who can determine the correct, safe dosage for you. Because Warfarin affects your blood clotting, any significant change in nutrient intake needs medical oversight to prevent dangerous side effects. Please schedule a quick telehealth appointment or call your pharmacist to get safe, personalized advice.",
